<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33120" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτῠπ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>model</i> or <i>work in relief</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῷ βάθρῳ τὰ ἑαυτοῦ ἔργα
					ἐξετύπωσεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Eq.</u>
					1.1
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐν στήλαις ἐκτετυπωμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Smp.</u>
					193a
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ti.</u>
				50d
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ ἐκτυπωθέντες</span>
			<i>these who are formed on this model</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Isoc.
				13.18
			</span></i>; <i>to be shaped</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τῇ διεξόδῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hp.
					<u>Prorrh.</u>
					2.4
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς τὸν Πρίαπον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Eus.
				<u>PE</u>
				3.11
			</span></i>; of the foetus, <i><span class="en">
				Agath.
				4.25
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph. in 
				Med.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκτυποῦσθαί τι εἰς
			ὕδωρ</span>, etc., <i>form an image</i> of a thing in . .,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Tht.</u>
				206d
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Lg.</u>
				775d
			</span></i>.</div>
